//! **Discharging the iota residual.**
//!
//! The pre-pass iota premise has been carried as a hypothesis since the faithful
//! loop was built. In its blanket form it was *false* — quantified over every
//! pre-pass function, it let an arbitrary pre-pass fire the rule with the wrong
//! constructor's fields (`wh3_hiota_repair.rs`, `wh_hiota_repair.rs`).
//! Constraining the pre-pass to be sound made it true. This proves it.
//!
//! # Why it is true, structurally
//!
//! `whc_reduct` reads `kapp_args e` only through `list_take PREFIX_N` and
//! `list_drop (Nat.succ MAJOR_IDX)`, and reads `kapp_args wmajor` for the
//! constructor's fields. **A swap at index `MAJOR_IDX` is invisible to all
//! three.** So reducing the major in place reduces the whole term, the swapped
//! spine is a genuine iota redex, and transitivity closes it.
//!
//! Nothing here is `hnf`-shaped: no ordering, no `Le`, no normalisation, no
//! accessibility. Every step is a definitional unfold plus an existing
//! take/drop/append lemma.
//!
//! # Two things that came out cheaper than expected
//!
//! * Extending the plain-iota firing past MINIMAL spines is *easier*, not
//!   harder. `whc_fires_plain_minimal` carries a length hypothesis and burns
//!   `minimal_major_is_last`; dropping that and taking the positional fact as a
//!   hypothesis leaves a character-identical body. The trailing arguments need
//!   nothing, because `whc_reduct` re-applies `list_drop (Nat.succ MAJOR_IDX)`
//!   to them.
//! * No `Le` reasoning appears anywhere, because `MAJOR_IDX` is *syntactically*
//!   `Nat.add PREFIX_N (recmeta_num_indices meta)`, so the additive hypothesis
//!   is exactly what `list_take_len_of_head` concludes.
//!
//! # What the capstone carries after this
//!
//! `hnf3` — satisfiable, supplied for the whole rigid-headed class, open for a
//! major stuck for a non-rigid reason — and the accessibility witness, which is
//! **permanently** a hypothesis: total inhabitation is strong normalisation, and
//! SN is false for this calculus as reflected.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

use crate::spec::error::SpecError;
use crate::spec::Specification;

impl Specification {
    /// The spine lemmas, the swap-and-fire argument, and the discharge.
    pub(super) fn add_hiotap3_discharge(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_PAR_REDUCES_CD_STAR_SPINE,
            "par_reduces_cd_star_spine: reducing the HEAD of a spine reduces the whole spine, at any depth. A four-line ListType.rec whose cons arm is par_reduces_cd_star_app against refl. \\
\\
No pointwise list relation is needed and none was built: only the head of the trailing spine changes, so the statement is about apply_spine's head argument alone. par_reduces_c_spine_cong exists but is over par_reduces_c, the delta-free RecEnv relation — the wrong relation, not reusable. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_KAPP_FN_KAPP_FN,
            "kapp_fn_kapp_fn: kapp_fn is idempotent. Nine-arm KExpr.rec, eight refl arms. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_KAPP_ARGS_KAPP_FN_NIL,
            "kapp_args_kapp_fn_nil: a spine head carries no arguments. Nine-arm KExpr.rec, eight refl arms. Needed because the swapped spine is rebuilt on kapp_fn e. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_LIST_TAKE_LEN_OF_HEAD,
            "list_take_len_of_head: if the k-th element exists then the first k elements number exactly k. The arithmetic that makes the prefix-preservation step free. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_LIST_SPLIT_AT_HEAD,
            "list_split_at_head: a list splits at any position its element exists at — take k ++ (m :: drop (k+1)) is the list. The structural heart of the argument-swap. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_LIST_TAKE_APPEND_GEN,
            "list_take_append_gen: appending past the first k elements does not disturb them. The general form of list_take_append_le, which is singleton-append only and carries an Le guard. \\
\\
No Le reasoning is needed here at all, because MAJOR_IDX is SYNTACTICALLY Nat.add PREFIX_N (recmeta_num_indices meta) — so the additive hypothesis is exactly what list_take_len_of_head concludes. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_WHC_FIRES_PLAIN_GEN,
            "whc_fires_plain_gen: the five surviving lookups fire a PLAIN iota on the swapped spine, at an ARBITRARY spine rather than a minimal one. \\
\\
Extending past the minimal spine turned out to be easier, not harder: whc_fires_plain_minimal carries a length hypothesis and burns minimal_major_is_last to discharge the positional level. Drop that and take the positional fact as a hypothesis, and the body is character-identical. The trailing arguments need no new machinery because whc_reduct re-applies list_drop (Nat.succ MAJOR_IDX) to them, which the swap leaves alone. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_WHC3_IOTA_SOUND_AT,
            "whc3_iota_sound_at: the swap-and-fire argument, with the spine abstract. Reducing the major in place reduces the whole term (par_reduces_cd_star_spine over list_split_at_head), the swapped spine is a genuine iota redex (whc_fires_plain_gen), and transitivity closes it. \\
\\
WHY THE ARGUMENT WORKS AT ALL, structurally: whc_reduct reads kapp_args e only through list_take PREFIX_N and list_drop (Nat.succ MAJOR_IDX), and reads kapp_args wmajor for the constructor's fields. A swap at index MAJOR_IDX is invisible to all three. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_HIOTAP3_DISCHARGED,
            "hiotap3_discharged: THE ITERATED-IOTA RESIDUAL, DISCHARGED. It is no longer a hypothesis. \\
\\
This premise has been carried since the faithful loop was built, on both the two-way and three-way paths, and in its BLANKET form it was false — quantified over every pre-pass function, it let an arbitrary pre-pass fire the rule with the wrong constructor's fields. Constraining the pre-pass to be sound made it true; this proves it. \\
\\
The route: invert the six-level chain with iota_reduct_whc3_some_inv_type, use the pre-pass soundness hypothesis on the level-4 equation to reduce the major in place, and hand the swapped spine to whc3_iota_sound_at. \\
\\
CONSEQUENCE for the capstone: def_eq_fuel_complete_wh3_at_the_red_env_na_hw can now be applied with this in the hiotap3 slot, leaving hnf3 — satisfiable, supplied for the rigid class — and the accessibility witness, which is permanently a hypothesis because total inhabitation is strong normalisation and SN is FALSE for this calculus as reflected. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        Ok(())
    }
}

